 "criteria": [
  {
   "detail": "Cache rows 402695, workbook data rows 402695. Earliest begin 1995-08-07, earliest termination 2016-10-03: arrangements that ended before that date are not in the export, so stocks before 2016 count survivors only. 373922 of 402695 begin dates fall in January, April, July or October; the registry moves in quarterly windows.",
   "kind": "instrument",
   "name": "B158-1",
   "passed": true
  },
  {
   "detail": "Begins/terminations by quarter: 2019Q1 5730/2203, 2019Q2 6931/3109, 2019Q3 7713/2672, 2019Q4 7609/2580, 2020Q1 14685/3043, 2020Q2 10381/2946, 2020Q3 10570/2610, 2020Q4 10854/2777, 2021Q1 10279/2421, 2021Q2 6963/2735, 2021Q3 9611/2472, 2021Q4 8802/3659, 2022Q1 11481/3457, 2022Q2 10974/3658, 2022Q3 9691/4003, 2022Q4 9771/3641. Manufacturer restrictions start in 2020-07; terminations show no cluster after it and begins stay high. A restriction cuts the price, not the listing, so the registry does not record the closing side. No termination reason column exists; the comment field names none.",
   "kind": "own_reading",
   "name": "B158-2",
   "passed": true
  },
  {
   "detail": "Arkansas pharmacies, new arrangements from covered entities in other states: 11 in the eight quarters before Rule 123 (effective 2022-09-30), 1689 in the eight from it. Around the statute date (2021-07-28): 9 and 517. Top pharmacy in the quarters after: 2022Q4 WAL-MART PHARMACY 10-0004 / SILOAM SPRINGS x1; 2023Q1 WALMART PHARMACY 10-5169 / ROGERS x23; 2023Q2 WALMART PHARMACY 10-5169 / ROGERS x463; 2023Q3 WALMART PHARMACY 10-5169 / ROGERS x516; 2023Q4 WALMART PHARMACY 10-5169 / ROGERS x202; 2024Q1 WALMART PHARMACY 10-5169 / ROGERS x270; 2024Q2 WALMART PHARMACY 10-5169 / ROGERS x137. These are registrations; whether manufacturers honoured the price on them is not read.",
   "kind": "own_reading",
   "name": "B158-3",
   "passed": true
  },
  {
   "detail": "The Rogers pharmacy (10-5169) holds Arkansas retail licence AR20927 issued 2020-03-23. Arrangements naming it between that date and 2022-09-30: 0; first begin 2023-01-01; 2408 arrangements from 2343 entities. The same entities at the chain's Texas central fill site (10-2670): Spring still active 1788; Spring ended before or on the Rogers begin 20; Spring ended after the Rogers begin 442; no Spring arrangement 93. The jump lines up with the rule date, not with the licence.",
   "kind": "own_reading",
   "name": "B158-4",
   "passed": true
  },
  {
   "detail": "Twenty-two laws, out-of-state begins eight quarters before and after the effective date, by the reach of the text: entity: 5 states, 2170 before, 1315 after; open text, effective 2024 or later: 11 states, 2594 before, 2203 after; pharmacy: 6 states, 863 before, 2323 after. Rows: AR 11->1689; LA 372->383; MS 191->225; MD 257->145; WV 106->49; MN 118->134; MO 729->698; NE 21->120; TN 1680->1527; UT 56->58; VT 64->4; HI 232->55; SD 0->3; ND 7->12; CO 43->27; ME 31->35; OR 78->24; RI 24->6; OK 39->13; NM 2->2; WA 377->231; IL 1189->401. No row carries a verdict. Open-text laws effective 2024 or later meet a manufacturer practice that already required both entity and pharmacy in the state.",
   "kind": "own_reading",
   "name": "B158-5",
   "passed": true
  },
  {
   "detail": "Distinct pharmacy addresses active at year end: 2010 1067 (GAO about 1300; survivors only, so at most that); 2017 19546 (GAO nearly 20000, ratio 0.977).",
   "kind": "known_answer",
   "name": "B158-6",
   "passed": true
  }
 ],
